<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:36:38Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ukraine, South Korea relations sour over North Korean POWs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fe2cd8368a330daa0ee68316fc89c5f4ea02eb924be4f4f9affa5248b3b33a4</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:36:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T02:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-south-korea-relations-sour-over-north-korean-pows/a-79451515--af4e1d864b6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-south-korea-relations-sour-over-north-korean-pows/a-79451515?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Korea has accused Ukraine of breaching a confidentiality agreement over the transfer of North Korean prisoners of war — and of denying the deal's existence. Seoul has demanded an apology.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israel strips Dutch diplomats of status in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9f329d448487f4bef11cea3fd2be73c0fa72bfc626de23b85766a588955c45b</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:36:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-28T00:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-strips-dutch-diplomats-of-status-in-west-bank/a-79451271--2548c1a9b002.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-strips-dutch-diplomats-of-status-in-west-bank/a-79451271?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The move by the Israeli Foreign Ministry is a response to Dutch sanctions targeting goods from illegal Israeli settlements in the occupied West Bank. The Dutch Foreign Ministry is yet to comment.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian President Aleksandar Vucic announces resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca1260a6995821a075b09e947a96f5acbfbb27ee56b22469d9e02a70bcac264a</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbian-president-aleksandar-vucic-announces-resignation/a-79450358--be764c7d61dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbian-president-aleksandar-vucic-announces-resignation/a-79450358?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Aleksandar Vucic will now be running to be prime minister in the upcoming snap parliamentary elections slated for next month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Houthis report deadly Saudi strikes on Taiz market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:835b43dcde944d2921c853f7a0b622a16e39af7b6691869d9e2cb84cd1bc69ed</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthis-report-deadly-saudi-strikes-on-taiz-market/a-79450102--5a221ceea050.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthis-report-deadly-saudi-strikes-on-taiz-market/a-79450102?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Houthi-run health ministry accused the Saudi Air Force of committing an "abominable crime," vowing to retaliate. The Houthis' account of the attack cannot be independently verified.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Avalanche in Nepal leaves 2 dead, several missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5349b3ccd5a356eaf48bd3a18862af477d447357c19b1253750d04c9970cbde7</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T17:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/avalanche-in-nepal-leaves-2-dead-several-missing/a-79450101--fcbca2d1e804.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/avalanche-in-nepal-leaves-2-dead-several-missing/a-79450101?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An avalanche has struck the Himlung Himal base camp in Nepal after days of severe weather. Two guides are confirmed dead and at least 14 people remain missing in the remote region.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK: 5 arrested after 'major incident' near Fairford air base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45fa282ee661d1e06959ac4ed0bad49196b2c2e1efd7cfd021e1e896c8c69ee4</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T17:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-5-arrested-after-major-incident-near-fairford-air-base/a-79447992--072dcc5d3fc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-5-arrested-after-major-incident-near-fairford-air-base/a-79447992?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Scores of homes were evacuated in the UK town of Whelford, near an air base used by the US military, with bomb disposal teams checking "suspicious vehicles" at the scene. Police said five men had been arrested.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Two people killed as bus crashes on way to Oktoberfest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9592ec5eb12f13f58d47f1ac5873e613f12c0f9e9f99eac41c19b5f73b475551</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T15:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/two-people-killed-as-bus-crashes-on-way-to-oktoberfest/a-79450016--d10b8bca83ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/two-people-killed-as-bus-crashes-on-way-to-oktoberfest/a-79450016?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bus was traveling from Italy to Munich, carrying 33 Filipino tourists who wanted to visit the famous beer festival. One of the dozens injured remains in life-threatening condition.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pope decries 'scourge' of sexual abuse during France visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:932271c194230fd39441bc35f6bdc027fa1bbf66015a58f40efd2ff8498b657e</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-decries-scourge-of-sexual-abuse-during-france-visit/a-79449335--995ba7f8239c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-decries-scourge-of-sexual-abuse-during-france-visit/a-79449335?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French bishops took "courageous" steps when faced with "the painful scourge of abuse of minors," Pope Leo XIV told the high-ranking clerics before his scheduled meeting with survivors at the Catholic shrine of Lourdes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>European cities seek ways of boosting affordable housing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:87fcfcd9657f7d172441312cab63125c7892812156eb70eec8c8c1a4b1667e69</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-cities-seek-ways-of-boosting-affordable-housing/a-79438939--fc67dbf8271c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-cities-seek-ways-of-boosting-affordable-housing/a-79438939?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In many major urban centers of Europe, the housing shortage has become an explosive social issue. DW looks into various models that have been put in place across the continent.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Switzerland: Voters reject stricter view of neutrality</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:243029d273a0bc70489dc2d0afca346e45afe8b303192220d25ee8ab53077dcf</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/switzerland-voters-reject-stricter-view-of-neutrality/a-79446996--5986041c2b6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/switzerland-voters-reject-stricter-view-of-neutrality/a-79446996?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Early projections show Swiss voters rejecting a stricter application of the country's vaunted neutrality. Swiss neutrality has been enshrined in the constitution since 1848.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Are Germans giving up their beloved meat and sausages?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1aae9e5f07fd83e167b69f62e98a0b25a6dadbf26a3995c899b076aa23ed26f</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-are-germans-giving-up-their-beloved-meat-and-sausages/live-79441034--d9fb5f1aa888.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-are-germans-giving-up-their-beloved-meat-and-sausages/live-79441034?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germans used to be all about sausages and meat. While those do remain popular, things seem to be slowly changing. There also are new insights into the economic side of East Germany's espionage DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Northern Ireland: Pro-UK march to go through Catholic area</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a28fb42713604eb949ba0d5b3b2493298ae6b73f952960b07ebad50584bb6a0</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/northern-ireland-pro-uk-march-to-go-through-catholic-area/a-79447441--5aa601872486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/northern-ireland-pro-uk-march-to-go-through-catholic-area/a-79447441?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's the first time the march has been allowed to go through the area since 1997. Overnight, a court ruling allowed it to take place after a series of last-minute legal challenges that reached Belfast's High Court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Kolkata's SRFTI students allege violent attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dce8adffb6d5c90fd3c49ec7103088f693bf3eacad591ca13d4a21e0f774a445</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-s-srfti-students-allege-violent-attack/live-79440869--92d965222a7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-s-srfti-students-allege-violent-attack/live-79440869?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Students at Kolkata's Satyajit Ray Film and Television Institute say they were attacked with knives after confronting an outside group over a meeting they allege was affiliated with the right-wing Hindu RSS.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran sticks to Hormuz plan after Trump rejects it</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ccc6feddf4e3e746ed338a113488fa6b25875b545108f11657aa06bb240e0841</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-sticks-to-hormuz-plan-after-trump-rejects-it/a-79447432--8e8b9e348264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-sticks-to-hormuz-plan-after-trump-rejects-it/a-79447432?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian officials that while they were aware of Trump's comments on rejecting the new proposal, they had not received a formal message rejecting the plan that would open the Strait of Hormuz.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>No public mentions of Taiwan at official Xi and Trump meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a81d407ff18138ab74a7579aa95724294095a6d734a64135fe002205d4d6ed57</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-public-mentions-of-taiwan-at-official-xi-and-trump-meeting/a-79445378--29352cbff0b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-public-mentions-of-taiwan-at-official-xi-and-trump-meeting/a-79445378?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At a high-profile summit between Presidents Donald Trump and Xi Jinping in Washington, there was much talk of trade and artificial intelligence. One of the most contentious issues, Taiwan, was only discussed in private.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China sends two giant pandas off to Atlanta zoo after Xi-Trump summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e9441e8384c31eb83da11e897c5c31206f9c9a056ee0dd237c2dbeb33c7236c</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T07:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-sends-two-giant-pandas-off-to-atlanta-zoo-after-xi-trump-summit/a-79447128--ab8e1682ffd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-sends-two-giant-pandas-off-to-atlanta-zoo-after-xi-trump-summit/a-79447128?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ping Ping and Fu Shuang took off to Atlanta on a FedEx plane, with steamed corn buns, carrots and bamboo to snack on during the flight. Their trip is one of the few concrete things to come out the Xi-Trump summit.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gunmen kill 27 people in two mass shootings in South Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc5b723d67441a2d0e84a7305e1f4eca76e693c6dad6d593b0e457f1df4dbc48</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T06:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gunmen-kill-27-people-in-two-mass-shootings-in-south-africa/a-79447130--f3bd024a1578.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gunmen-kill-27-people-in-two-mass-shootings-in-south-africa/a-79447130?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South African police have launched a search for suspects after 17 people were found dead at a tavern southwest of Johannesburg. A separate tavern shooting near Cape Town left 10 dead.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why farmers are pairing crops with solar panels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc55fd6d221118fc60a690ffb9aa0dbbe0351a4ee4fb78cacbf68081428912a8</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T04:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-farmers-are-pairing-crops-with-solar-panels/a-79233970--008efaae1ed6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-farmers-are-pairing-crops-with-solar-panels/a-79233970?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From cooler soil to paid grazing land, farmers in the US are finding that solar panels can do more than generate power.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Powerful storm batters northeast US, hundreds of flights canceled</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:213a44c8b6d738f7b9e0a9f91158f93cbede45365d7e60c3ee4bdbf9d6f766e8</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T03:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/powerful-storm-batters-northeast-us-hundreds-of-flights-canceled/a-79446676--6ec8e25a25ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/powerful-storm-batters-northeast-us-hundreds-of-flights-canceled/a-79446676?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of flights were canceled and thousands were delayed as a nor'easter brought flooding, power cuts and travel disruption to cities like New York, Boston and Philadelphia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Thousands protest in Madrid against housing crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:738264de6c0c9c037929c64e434384dcb3fb06d0969d2963ff4bbb8c4b8e88b3</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T01:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-thousands-protest-in-madrid-against-housing-crisis/a-79446662--133b5faee12d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-thousands-protest-in-madrid-against-housing-crisis/a-79446662?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands rallied in the Spanish capital after an 87-year-old woman was dramatically evicted from her home this week. Protesters called for measures to curb rising costs and reduce evictions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Backlash over data centers tests Europe's AI ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e685f3c48548164b20286e359f17eea48065503633af28be8805f0e0d8e2bdbd</id><updated>2026-09-28T05:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T18:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800--224361aa983d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Massive data centers needed to run AI are triggering protests across Europe. Their operators counter that they boost digital sovereignty and energy independence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
